---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const muso = 'https://credits.muso.ai/search?keyword=Eric%20Sarafin';
---
<Base title="Mixing — Mixerman"
  description="Gold and platinum mixing, mastering, and production by Mixerman (Eric Sarafin) — over a billion streams across numerous genres, delivered from an acoustically accurate room in Asheville, NC."
  image="/uploads/2025/08/Screenshot-2025-08-20-at-9.00.51-AM.webp">

  <!-- TITLE BAND -->
  <section class="section section--deep" style="padding:40px 0 28px">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <div class="lineband">
        <h1 class="plate" style="font-size:clamp(1.4rem, 2.8vw, 2rem)">Mixing</h1>
      </div>
      <img src="/brand/services-tape.webp" alt="Mixing • Production • Recording • Mastering" width="510"
        style="display:block; margin:12px auto 0; max-width:88%; height:auto; transform:rotate(-1.2deg)" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE CONTROL ROOM: Ben Harper, Mixerman, JP Plunier -->
  <section class="mixband">
    <figure>
      <img class="mixband-photo" src="/uploads/2022/09/mm-jp-and-ben-band.webp"
        alt="JP Plunier, Mixerman, and Ben Harper seated at the console at Alpha Studios" width="2560" height="1105" />
      <figcaption>From left to right: JP Plunier, Mixerman, Ben Harper — Alpha Studios, 1999, recording <em>Burn to Shine</em>.<br />Incidentally, I started posting on Usenet as Mixerman while making this album.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- TRACK RECORD -->
  <section class="section" style="padding:44px 0 10px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lineband lineband--thin" style="text-align:center">
        <h2 class="plate">Track Record</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:980px">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:44px">
        <a class="float-badge" href={muso} target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="View my full discography on Muso.ai">
          <img src="/uploads/2026/09/muso-summary.webp"
            alt="Muso.ai summary card — Eric Sarafin, engineer, producer, musician: 1.1 billion streams, 481 credits, 294 thousand videos, 429 million views"
            width="800" height="1001" />
        </a>
        <p style="padding-top:12px">With over a billion streams and millions of records sold, I have multiple gold and platinum records across numerous genres.</p>
        <p class="roster">Of course, quality of work is just as important as success. You want your record to be the best it can be. As do I. Given this, you can expect the same level of work from me that I've provided artists like The Pharcyde, Spearhead, Ben Harper, Ian Moore, Lifehouse, Barenaked Ladies, Foreigner, and Australian phenom Pete Murray, just to name a few.</p>
        <p class="roster"><a href={muso} target="_blank" rel="noopener">See my full discography.</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACCURACY -->
  <section class="section section--deep" style="padding-top:44px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lineband lineband--thin" style="text-align:center">
        <h2 class="plate">Accuracy</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:980px">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
        <span class="float-room">
          <img src="/uploads/2025/08/Mix-Room.webp"
            alt="Mixerman's mix and production suite in Asheville, NC — tapestried walls, string lights, and monitors at the mix position"
            width="941" height="941" />
          <i class="tape tape--tl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--tr" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--bl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--br" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </span>
        <p>I can tell you from experience, you can't mix well in any old room. I purpose-built my mix and production room, which is acoustically tuned and features Dutch &amp; Dutch 8c monitors that adapt to the room using cardioid technology. This allows me to deliver fully mastered mixes with perfect accuracy and predictable translation. From the very first bounce, you’re hearing your record as it’s meant to sound, with no guessing about how it will translate later. This makes the notes process far more efficient and satisfying.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MUSICALITY -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-bottom:44px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lineband lineband--thin" style="text-align:center">
        <h2 class="plate">Musicality</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:980px">
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
        <span class="float-piano">
          <img src="/uploads/2026/08/wing-and-son-piano.webp"
            alt="A Wing &amp; Son upright piano with its front open, beside a vintage electric piano and a row of microphone stands"
            width="1600" height="1194" />
          <i class="tape tape--p1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--p2" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--p3" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="tape tape--p4" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </span>
        <p style="display:flow-root">I studied piano with jazz legend Kenny Barron and went to Berklee College of Music, so I place a premium on musicality in every decision I make, whether it’s mixing or mastering. My work is based entirely on what you’ve already accomplished with your production and song. My job is to maximize your track’s impact and to enhance lift. That’s what makes for a successful record that people will enjoy again and again.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REACH OUT -->
  <section class="section section--deep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lineband lineband--thin" style="text-align:center">
        <h2 class="plate">Reach Out</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:980px">
      <div class="reach">
        <div class="prose" style="margin:0">
          <p style="text-align:left">If you’d like to chat about your project, <br />use the contact portal to get in touch.</p>
          <p style="text-align:left; margin-top:.8em">Or email me directly at {/* Underlined, and in the deep red: on this beige band no red can both stand
              3:1 from the ink and read 4.5:1 against the ground, so the line does
              the distinguishing and the darker red does the reading. */}
          <a href="mailto:mixerman@mixerman.net" style="white-space:nowrap; color:var(--red-deep); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px">mixerman@mixerman.net</a>.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1.4em"><a class="btn btn--red" href="/about-contact/">Request a Quote</a></p>
        </div>
        <img class="envelope" src="/uploads/2026/08/mmpub-envelope-stamp.webp"
          alt="A kraft envelope bearing the Mixerman Publishes yin-yang postage stamp, postmarked Asheville, NC"
          width="1200" height="1200" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The homepage mixerband's frame: photo centred on an ink band, a shade
     over 1032px so it stands wider than the text column. The photo is muted
     toward the site's black-and-white; Eric's crop is baked into the file. */
  .mixband { background: var(--ink); border-bottom: 4px solid var(--ink); }
  .mixband figure { margin: 0; }
  .mixband-photo {
    display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 1032px; margin: 0 auto;
    height: auto;
    filter: grayscale(.85) brightness(.82);
  }
  /* the caption types itself on the ink under the photo, quiet and centred */
  .mixband figcaption {
    max-width: 1032px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 10px 24px 14px;
    font-family: var(--type);
    font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--cream); opacity: .85;
    text-align: left;
  }

  /* this page's copy runs a tad wider than the site's 700px measure, so the
     text blocks square up better with the pictures floated in them.
     flow-root makes each block own its floated picture, so section padding
     measures from whichever runs lower. Set copy, like a book page — with
     book rules: a hyphen needs 3 letters before it and 4 after (no
     "acoustical-ly", no "al-lows"), and never two hyphenated lines in a
     row (the lines rule is honoured by Safari; others ignore it). */
  .prose { max-width: 760px; display: flow-root; }
  .prose p {
    text-align: justify;
    hyphens: auto;
    hyphenate-limit-chars: 6 3 4;
    -webkit-hyphenate-limit-before: 3;
    -webkit-hyphenate-limit-after: 4;
    -webkit-hyphenate-limit-lines: 1;
    hyphenate-limit-lines: 1;
  }

  /* pictures float inside the prose column the way the homepage About photo
     does: wide bands, constrained copy, text wrapping the image */
  .float-badge {
    float: left;
    width: min(340px, 48%);
    margin: .3em 28px 12px 0;
  }
  /* on wide screens the badge borrows the gutter beside the reading measure,
     growing without costing the copy its column */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .float-badge { width: 380px; margin-left: -56px; }
  }
  /* the roster holds the right column whole — flow-root keeps its box beside
     the badge instead of letting lines slip raggedly underneath */
  .roster { display: flow-root; }
  /* each picture sits a touch off square, alternating lean like the site's
     tape strips — on the badge the tilt rides the inner image, so the
     link's hover lift doesn't straighten it */
  .float-badge img {
    display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 3px rgba(20, 16, 12, .45),
      5px 12px 28px rgba(20, 16, 12, .38);
  }
  /* the room hangs taped to the page: thrown further off square, nudged
     toward the gutter, a strip of scotch tape at each corner */
  .float-room {
    float: right; display: block; position: relative;
    width: min(300px, 42%);
    margin: .3em 0 12px 28px;
    transform: rotate(4.5deg) translateX(36px);
  }
  .float-room img {
    display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    /* 60% of the mixband photo's muting — colour dialed back, not gone */
    filter: grayscale(.51) brightness(.89);
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 3px rgba(20, 16, 12, .45),
      5px 12px 28px rgba(20, 16, 12, .38);
  }
  /* scotch tape: translucent strips, every piece its own length and lean */
  .tape {
    position: absolute; display: block;
    background: linear-gradient(rgba(255, 253, 244, .34), rgba(255, 253, 244, .22));
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(20, 16, 12, .22);
  }
  .tape--tl { width: 98px; height: 30px; top: 3px; left: -31px; transform: rotate(-43deg); }
  .tape--tr { width: 74px; height: 25px; top: 5px; right: -19px; transform: rotate(35deg); opacity: .85; }
  .tape--bl { width: 66px; height: 24px; bottom: 6px; left: -15px; transform: rotate(49deg); opacity: .9; }
  .tape--br { width: 108px; height: 31px; bottom: 2px; right: -36px; transform: rotate(-33deg); }
  .float-piano {
    float: left; display: block; position: relative;
    width: min(360px, 48%);
    margin: .3em 28px 12px 0;
    transform: rotate(-7deg) translate(-34px, 26px);
  }
  .float-piano img {
    display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    filter: grayscale(.51) brightness(.89);
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 3px rgba(20, 16, 12, .45),
      5px 12px 28px rgba(20, 16, 12, .38);
  }
  .tape--p1 { width: 94px; height: 28px; top: 4px; left: -29px; transform: rotate(-38deg); }
  .tape--p2 { width: 68px; height: 24px; top: 6px; right: -16px; transform: rotate(42deg); opacity: .85; }
  .tape--p3 { width: 100px; height: 30px; bottom: 3px; right: -32px; transform: rotate(-30deg); opacity: .93; }
  .tape--p4 { width: 80px; height: 26px; bottom: 5px; left: -22px; transform: rotate(40deg); opacity: .88; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .float-badge { float: none; display: block; width: min(320px, 100%); margin: 0 auto 1.2em; }
    /* the throws stay, the nudges don't — no room to spare on a phone */
    .float-room { float: none; width: min(300px, 100%); margin: 0 auto 1.2em; transform: rotate(4.5deg); }
    .float-piano { float: none; display: block; width: min(360px, 100%); margin: 0 auto 1.6em; transform: rotate(-7deg); }
  }

  /* the closing ask: copy and button on the left, the stamped envelope
     standing small at their right */
  .reach {
    display: flex; align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    max-width: 740px; margin: 30px auto 0;
  }
  .envelope {
    display: block; flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: min(210px, 34%); height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 3px rgba(20, 16, 12, .45),
      5px 12px 28px rgba(20, 16, 12, .38);
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .reach { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
    /* the two-line break is set for the wide layout; on a phone the
       sentence centers and wraps where it will */
    .reach .prose p { text-align: center; }
    .reach br { display: none; }
    .envelope { width: min(210px, 70%); }
  }
</style>
